4. NOT APPLIED — with reasons (for the supervisor)
================================================================================
 (i)  a#53 and b#13 — Swedish space-grouped thousands ("500 000 TWD", "25 000 000 TWD", "1.579.589" →
      "1 579 589"). BLOCKED BY THE CHECKER, not by judgement. scripts/check-column-translation.mjs sets
      NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE.sv = 'dot'; any space separator (U+0020, U+00A0, U+202F, U+2009, U+2007 — all
      tested) splits "500 000" into the tokens 500 and 0, so the source value 500000 goes missing and the
      file FAILs the numbers rule. The German-style "500.000" is therefore kept throughout 001–004, 006, 007,
      010, 011, 015, 017, 018. FIX REQUIRED UPSTREAM: add 'sv' (and da/nb/fi) to a space-thousands style in
      NUMBER_THOUSAND_STYLE, then this row can be applied mechanically. The decimal-comma half of the row WAS
      applied where the checker does not govern the text (guidance team bio: "1,57 miljoner TWD").
 (ii) a#38's month-name half — "den 29 maj 2026" is the natural Swedish form but DATE_MONTH_NAMES in the
      checker lacks the Swedish months maj, mars and augusti, so a month-name date silently drops the month
      number and FAILs. Applied the checker-safe variant (plain 2026-05-29 without "den"), which is standard
      Swedish. FIX REQUIRED UPSTREAM: add maj: 5, mars: 3, augusti: 8 to DATE_MONTH_NAMES.
 (iii) a#11 (005 body link) — the body still points at
      https://www.wei-wei-lawyer.com/post/%EB%8C%80%EB%A7%8C-%ED%9A%8C%EC%82%AC%EC%84%A4%EB%A6%BD-… (percent-
      encoded Hangul) instead of the English slug used in 001–004/006–007. ACCEPTED-sv says rows about the
      Hangul/percent-encoded wei-wei-lawyer.com body links are already fixed mechanically (R1) and are to be
      skipped — but in columns-sv/005 the old link is still live. Flagging it: it is a one-line href change
      (…/post/taiwan-company-establishment-advanced-1) that this lane did not make because ACCEPTED-sv told
      it to skip and because the checker byte-compares hrefs.
 (iv) b#9 (011 Invest Taiwan link lang=jpn) — same situation. ACCEPTED-sv says "fixed mechanically — skip",
      but columns-sv/011 still carries
      https://investtaiwan.nat.gov.tw/showPage?lang=jpn&search=InvestmentStatus01, i.e. a Swedish reader is
      sent to the Japanese UI, while 004 already uses lang=eng. Not changed (skip instruction + href parity);
      flagging for the supervisor.
 (v)  a#8's suggested wording — the reviewer wants the Swedish text to state the rate that applies to Swedish
      recipients ("För svenska mottagare gäller i stället intern taiwanesisk källskatt (i regel 21 %)"). Not
      applied as written: that is an affirmative tax statement about the reader's own jurisdiction, which
      RULEBOOK R2b and ACCEPTED-sv forbid ("Do NOT insert claims about the law of the reader's country") and
      which would also put a nationality into a block whose Korean source has none. The R2b framing sentence
      is used instead, and the pre-existing internal 21 % sentence is kept.
 (vi) a#16's suggested wording — "till exempel Sverige och Taiwan". Not applied: naming Sweden in a block
      whose source names only Korea makes the column checker's `nationality` rule FAIL (a nationality present
      in the target and absent from the aligned source block is a hard failure unless an adapt-log covers it).
      The neutral R2d formulation was used.
 (vii) a#32's suggested wording — "Ansvarsfriskrivning" as the nav label. Not applied: 19 characters, and
      guidance-hi-sv-da-nb-fi-content.test.ts caps every sv nav label at 14. Used "Friskrivning" (12).
 (viii) b#36's suggested wording — "artikel 7 första stycket 7". Not applied verbatim (deletes the digit 1
      the source requires); used "artikel 7, 1 stycket, punkt 7".
 (ix) b#39's suggested wording — bare "tillhör första arvsklassen". Not applied verbatim (same digit problem,
      confirmed by an actual FAIL run); used "tillhör första arvsklassen (rang 1)".
 (x)  a#23's optional gloss — adding (侵權行為) to the guidance services text was reverted: guidance-disclosure-
      parity.test.ts requires the same set of Chinese-character terms per surface across all locales, and the
      added gloss broke `services: sv annotates a different set of Chinese-character terms than vi`.
 (xi) "var 2:e månad" (001 §5) — left as is. "varannan månad" is the natural Swedish, but it deletes the
      digit 2 that the source carries. Same class of problem as (i)/(ii).

Nothing in either review was judged simply wrong on the Swedish; the only disagreements are the six wording
substitutions above, each of which is a checker/test constraint rather than a language call, plus a#8/a#16
where the reviewer's suggestion conflicts with the supervisor's own rulebook.
